      "words": 18
    },
    {
      "block": "原句4",
      "no": 4,
      "segments": [
        {
          "text": "But just like pushing over a lettuce, this is the tip of the iceberg",
          "ok": true,
          "pos": 363
        }
      ],
      "words": 14
    },
    {
      "block": "原句5",
      "no": 5,
      "segments": [
        {
          "text": "Like a naked cat attacking beachgoers, you’ve barely scratched the surfers",
          "ok": true,
          "pos": 433
        }
      ],
      "words": 11
    },
    {
      "block": "原句6",
      "no": 6,
      "segments": [
        {
          "text": "There are thousands of jokes about nuns, for instance, and this book doesn’t contain any – nun whatsoever",
          "ok": true,
          "pos": 601
        }
      ],
      "words": 18
    },
    {
      "block": "原句7",
      "no": 7,
      "segments": [
        {
          "text": "And there can be more, and, as the electrician said when he electrocuted a German woman’s son, the power is in your Hans",
          "ok": true,
          "pos": 707
        }
      ],
      "words": 23
    },
    {
      "block": "原句8",
      "no": 8,
      "segments": [
        {
          "text": "At their best, rubbish jokes can unite people – eye-rolls and reluctant grins transcend divides and help us progress as ",
          "ok": true,
          "pos": 828
        }
      ],
      "words": 21
    },
    {
      "block": "原句9",
      "no": 9,
      "segments": [
        {
          "text": "Before a bad joke we’re immature, but afterwards? Fully groan",
          "ok": true,
          "pos": 956
        }
